# An ALLOWLIST (plan §15g M8): everything is excluded, then exactly what the .vsix needs is let back in. A file added to
# src_vs_code/ ships only when it is named here — the opposite of a denylist, where a new folder (goldens, fixtures,
# research, a .vscode-test/ download) ships until somebody remembers to exclude it. CI holds `vsce ls --no-dependencies`
# equal to vsix-files.txt and unzips the built .vsix for paths, names, e-mail addresses, source maps and the build stamp
# (scripts/check-vsix.mjs).
**
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!dist/extension.js
# W0 of todo/PLAN_disk_health_E18.md: the full view's page script and the kit's stylesheet esbuild emits beside it — exactly these two
!dist/webview/full.js
!dist/webview/full.css
# E7.S5a: the attested Windows daemon, fetched and verified (scripts/fetch-windows-daemon.mjs) — never its .sha256, never anything else in bin/
!bin/wsl-care.exe
!media/**
